## 1. Scope
The baseline is a classic MOBA rule set. Every system is either part of this baseline or listed as a Brainrot original.

| Core rules | Brainrot originals |
| --- | --- |
| Level cap 25 | Clout (signature resource) |
| Ultimates unlock at 6, 11, 16 | Go Viral |
| Four abilities, three attributes | Stan (creep buff) |
| Lanes, towers, content mills, Original Post | Ratio (death transfer) |
| Boss objective with a revive reward | Repost chain |
| Delivery Drone, shops, wards, day/night | Rebrand |
| Ultimate upgrade item | Go Private (padlock) |
| Attribute stat rules | The Trend and Screenshot |
| Gold, XP, bounties | Parasocial tether |

Remix policy: a Brainrot original may only sit in the slot of a classic system (see section 2). It may add a decision. It may not add a new resource that nobody can read. Numbers marked verify are set in the balance pass.

## 2. Vision and pillars
6.88 Brainrot is a caricature MOBA. Every hero, item and creep is drawn to be read at a glance, and rewards a second look. The game runs on a classic MOBA decision set. The jokes ride on top of it.

The AI theme is satire of the feed, not of a real product. The AI items (section 11) carry it.

Four rules every system must pass:

1. **Readable.** A player can tell what a unit or item does from its silhouette and color, without reading text.
2. **Decisive.** Each system creates a choice with a cost on each side.
3. **Mapped.** Each system holds the job of a classic system (table below). A system needs a classic job to earn its place.
4. **Off the read path.** Jokes live in tooltips, announcers, idle animations and marginalia. They never hide a gameplay signal.

| Classic job | Brainrot system | Decision it creates |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Last hitting | Engagement farming: +1 Clout when in enemy hero vision | Farm in fog for gold, or in sight for gold, Clout and risk |
| Denying | Ratio deny: takes 0.5 Clout from the nearest enemy hero watching the creep | Contest the creep for gold, or drain enemy Clout |
| Vision and wards | Audience: enemy heroes give Clout. Enemy wards reveal, earn nothing. | Warding reveals the enemy at no Clout cost |
| Creep wave pressure | Stan: allied creeps inside Reach gain damage and armor | Stand with the wave to push, or rotate and lose the buff |
| Map pressure, rotation | Go Viral: 20 s spike with global reveal | Spend the spike on a siege, or hold it as a threat |
| Boss objective and revive reward | The Trend and Screenshot | Contest the pit, or trade it for towers |
| Patch meta | Trend modifiers, rotating each patch | Draft and itemize for the modifier |
| Teamfight chain | Repost chain | Group to chain the buff, or spread against AoE |
| Comeback gold | Ratio transfer on death | A leader cannot take risky fights for free |
| Glyph | Go Private: buildings invulnerable 5 s, 5 min cooldown | Timing of the emergency button in a siege |
| Buyback | Rebrand: costs gold, resets Clout to 0 | Respawn now with no Clout, or wait with Clout intact |
| Support tether | Parasocial tether: 20% of an ally's Clout is shared | Stan the carry for safety, or the roamer for pressure |

## 3. Core loop and win condition
Two teams of five. Each team defends a base, a set of lanes, and an Original Post. Destroying the enemy Original Post wins the match.

### Lanes and structures

| Structure | Per side | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tier 1 tower | 3 (one per lane) | Armor aura for allied heroes: +1 |
| Tier 2 tower | 3 | Armor aura: +3. Invulnerable until its T1 falls. |
| Tier 3 tower | 3 | Armor aura: +3. Damage equal to T2. |
| Tier 4 towers | 2 (at the Original Post) | Invulnerable until a T3 falls in any lane |
| Content Mills | 6 (two per lane, melee and ranged) | A lane with both its Content Mills down spawns Super creeps; a destroyed mill respawns after 5 min (UNVERIFIED) |
| All six Content Mills down | n/a | Mega creeps spawn in all three lanes until a mill respawns |
| Original Post | 1 | Invulnerable until both T4s fall. Destroying it wins. |

- Tower HP: T1 1,300, T2 1,600, T3 1,600, T4 2,200. Gold per tower: 160, 200, 240, 280.
- Towers regenerate and take reduced damage when no enemy creeps are nearby (backdoor protection).
- Go Private (padlock): makes all team buildings invulnerable for 5 s. Cooldown 5 min. It refreshes when a T1 falls.

### Creep waves

- A wave spawns every 30 s: three melee and one ranged per lane.
- A siege creep joins every fifth wave.
- Creeps upgrade every 7.5 min: +12 HP and +2 gold per upgrade.
- Aggro: attacking an enemy hero draws nearby creeps for 2.5 s, with a 2.5 s cooldown.

### Match flow

1. Draft (section 14). Players spawn at the Spawn Lounge. Creeps spawn at 0:00.
2. Laning, 0:00 to about 10:00. Farm, deny, trade, ward.
3. Rotations and objectives. The Trend opens at about 10:00 (section 12).
4. Pushing. Break T1s, then T2s and T3s, then content mills.
5. Original Post. The team that breaks the Original Post wins.

Surrender rule: at 30 minutes, a team can vote to surrender with 4 of 5 players agreeing. Voting resets after each failed vote, and a vote is open once per 5 minutes.

## 4. Map
The map is two halves split by a river. Each half holds three lanes, a jungle and a base.

### Bases

- **Morning Feed** (ally): light value, sunrise palette. The river is the Feed, with slow caustics.
- **Late Night Feed** (enemy): dark value, screen glow.
- Each base holds the Spawn Lounge, a main shop at the Spawn Lounge, one Back Alley Shop, two Side Shops (one each on the top and bottom lanes), and a Trending Pit.

### Lanes

Three lanes per team: top, mid and bottom. Lane assignment by role is in section 14. Side Shops sit at the lane mouths and sell basic components.

### River

- The river splits the map. It holds the two boost spots and the Trend pit.
- Two boost spots on the river. Boosts spawn every 2 min (section 12).
- Shallow crossings let heroes cross the river at fixed points only.

### Jungle

Each team has a primary and a secondary jungle.

| Jungle | Camps | Stack rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary | 2 hard, 2 medium, 1 small | Pulled camps respawn on the minute |
| Secondary | 1 hard, 1 elder | Elders are magic-resistant, not spell-immune (see section 12) |
| Near Back Alley Shop | 1 hard | Guards the Back Alley Shop approach |

Jungle creature names are in section 12.

### Structure list

Towers, Content Mills, Original Post and Spawn Lounge are in section 3. Shops, inventory and items are in section 11. Wards are in section 13.

### Map props and marginalia

Out-of-bounds marginalia (ten static vignettes) sit on the map edge. They never block movement and never hide a unit. Full list in section 18.

## 5. Economy
There are three currencies: gold (spent), XP (levels), and Clout (section 6, a Brainrot original). Gold is split into reliable gold (kills, towers, The Trend, bounties) and unreliable gold (creep income). Dying loses only unreliable gold.

### Gold

| Source | Value | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Starting gold | 600 | Fixed value |
| Passive income | 1 gold per second | Gold each second alive |
| Lane creep last hit | Melee 38-48, ranged 43-53, siege 66-80 | Unreliable. Wave composition in section 3 (UNVERIFIED) |
| Hero kill | 110 + streak bounty + level × 9.9 | Reliable |
| Assist, AoE share | 1 hero: 150 + 6L · 2: 100 + 5L · 3: 40 + 4L · 4: 25 + 3L · 5: 20 + 3L | L is the victim's level. Shared across heroes in range. |
| Streak bounty | 60 up to 480 at a long streak | Ends on death |
| Tower | Team gold per tier (about 160, 200, 240, 280) | Denied tower = 50%. |
| Lurker Cam kill | 100 gold, 25 XP | Enemy ward, section 13 |

### Death and respawn

- **Death cost:** 30 × hero level, taken from unreliable gold.
- **Respawn:** 5 + 3.8 × level seconds (8.8 s at level 1, 100 s at level 25).
- **Ratio on death:** the victim loses 50% of Clout (section 6), split among killers and assists.

### Rebrand

- **Cost:** 100 + 1.5 × level² + 0.25 × game seconds. Spends reliable gold first.
- **Effect:** a Rebrand resets Clout to 0 and ends the respawn timer early.
- **Penalty:** no unreliable gold until the normal respawn timer would have ended. 25% of the skipped timer is added to the next death.
- **Cooldown:** 6 min (360 s).

### Experience

Hero kill XP: 100, 120, 140, 160, 180 for levels 1 to 5, then 100 more per level. Shared among heroes in range. Denied lane creeps give 50% of their XP to the enemy team. Neutral-denied creeps give 35%.

Total XP to reach each level (cumulative, lookup values):

| Level | Total XP | Level | Total XP |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2 | 200 | 15 | 11,900 |
| 5 | 1,400 | 20 | 20,900 |
| 10 | 5,400 | 25 | 32,400 |

### Clock

- Creeps spawn at 0:00.
- Neutrals spawn at 0:30 and every minute after.
- Boosts spawn every 2 min.
- The Trend opens at about 10:00.
- Bounty boosts spawn at the river at game start, four in total.

## 6. Clout
Clout is the signature resource. A hero earns Clout only while an enemy hero can see them. It is the reason to stay in the open, and the reason to be ratioed when you are.

### Earning Clout

| Action | Clout | Condition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Last hit | +1 | Inside enemy hero vision |
| Deny | +0.5 | Taken from the nearest enemy hero, while that hero sees the creep |
| Hero kill | +10 | None |
| Assist | +4 | None |
| Tower damage | +1 per 100 damage | While an enemy hero sees the tower |
| Enemy ward | 0 | Reveals the warded area, earns nothing |
| Any action unseen | 0 | Gold and XP still earned |

### Clout rules

| Rule | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Reach radius | 300 + 3 × Clout, capped at 600 |
| Stan | Allied creeps inside Reach: +20% damage, +2 armor |
| Go Viral threshold | 100 Clout |
| Go Viral duration | 20 s |
| Go Viral effects | Reach +200; lane spawns +1 melee creep per wave; caster revealed on the global minimap |
| Clout after Go Viral | 25 |
| Ratio on death | Victim loses 50% of Clout, split among killer and assists |
| Decay | Above 50 Clout: −1 every 10 s while unseen for those 10 s |
| Cap on Ratio | At most 200 Clout moves in one death |

### Clout states

Each hero is in one of four states at any time. The state sets what the rest of the map can see.

1. **Quiet.** Below 50 Clout, no enemy vision. Earns gold and XP only.
2. **LIVE.** An enemy hero has the hero in vision. The violet LIVE dot shows on the portrait. Clout is earned.
3. **Viral.** At 100 Clout. Go Viral is active for 20 s. The hero is revealed on the global minimap.
4. **Ratioed.** Death. Clout transfers to the killer and assists. The hero returns to Quiet at spawn.

Rebrand resets a hero to Quiet at 0 Clout.

### Design rules

- Clout is never a stat. It never adds damage or armor directly. Its only effects are Reach, Go Viral, Stan and the Algorithm mood.
- Clout is never shared between teams. The ally tether (section 2) shares a fraction of an ally's Clout, and only with that ally.
- Clout is shown as one number on the top bar, abbreviated (1.2K) and exact on hover.

### Algorithm mood

Each team has one mood, set by the gap between the two teams' total Clout. Mood changes Reach and minimap reveal only. It is not a stat and never adds damage or armor. Numbers are UNVERIFIED.

| Mood | Entered when | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Front Runner | Team total ahead by 300 Clout or more for 30 s | Its heroes get Reach +50. Its highest-Clout hero shows on the minimap as a Front Runner icon for 20 s every 60 s. |
| Underdog | Team total behind by 300 Clout or more for 30 s | Its heroes get Reach +50. It captures Breaking News zones at double speed (section 12). |
| Even | Neither of the above | No effect. |

A mood ends when the gap falls below 150 Clout for 30 s, so moods do not flicker.

## 7. Heroes and attributes
Every hero has three attributes, a primary attribute, and a base stat block. Heroes level to 25.

### Attributes

| Attribute | Per point | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Strength | +20 max HP, +0.1 HP regen | Melee durability |
| Agility | +1 attack speed, +1/7 armor | Armor per point is 1/7 |
| Intelligence | +12 max mana, +0.05 mana regen, +1% spell amp per 16 INT | Spell amp is additive with item amp |

Primary attribute: +1 damage per point of the primary attribute. There is no Universal attribute.

### Base stats

| Stat | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Base HP | 200 |
| Base mana | 50 |
| Base movement speed | 300 |
| Maximum movement speed | 522 |
| Melee attack range | 150 |
| Ranged attack range | 500 default, 300 to 700 |
| Base attack time (BAT) | 1.7 melee, 1.5 ranged |
| Turn rate | 0.6 s |
| Magic resistance | 25% base |

Each hero can override the base attack time and turn rate. These two values define the hero's feel.

### Level

- Level cap: 25. Level comes from XP (section 5).
- Ability points: one per level, plus the ultimate unlock rule.
- Ultimates unlock at levels 6, 11 and 16. They max at level 3.
- Standard abilities max at level 4.
- Level 25 is the final level. There is no stat skill for leftover points.

### Respawn

Heroes respawn at their Spawn Lounge. Respawn time is 5 + 3.8 × level seconds (section 5). Heroes spawn with full health and mana.

### Hero shape

Every hero is one of three silhouettes: circle (support), square (durable), triangle (aggressive or mobile). Hero archetype, silhouette and shape language are in section 17.

## 8. Combat rules
### Damage types

| Type | Reduced by | Blocked by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Physical | Armor | Evasion, miss chance |
| Magical | Magic resistance | Spell immunity |
| Pure | Nothing | Nothing |
| HP removal | Nothing | Nothing; HP removal ignores spell immunity |

### Armor and magic resistance

- Physical damage multiplier: 1 − (0.06 × A) / (1 + 0.06 × |A|), where A is armor. Negative armor amplifies damage.
- Magic resistance: heroes start at 25%. Each source multiplies. Two sources at 25% each give 1 − 0.75 × 0.75 = 43.75%.

### Attack speed

- Attacks per second = (100 + bonus attack speed) / (BAT × 100).
- Total attack speed is capped at 600.
- Attack animation: attack point, then backswing. Animation canceling is allowed.

### Evasion and miss

- Evasion uses pseudo-random distribution, checked on impact.
- Miss chance (for example, uphill attacks) is separate from evasion.
- True strike ignores evasion. Sources: specific items and the Hot Take archetype.

### Lifesteal and amplification

- Attack lifesteal: items and a few hero abilities.
- Spell lifesteal: none in v1.
- Spell amplification: Intelligence (section 7) plus one item.
- Cooldown reduction: Refresh Page (cooldown reset) and the Unboxing modifier only.

### Disables

| Disable | Effect | Break rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Stun | No actions or movement | Stun cannot be broken |
| Polymorph | Transforms the target | Dispelled by strong dispel |
| Silence | No abilities, items still work | Strong dispel removes it |
| Root | No movement, abilities work | Dispelled by basic dispel |
| Sleep | Stun that breaks on damage | Breaks on any damage |
| Taunt | Forced to attack the source | Lasts its duration |
| Disarm | No attacks, abilities work | Dispelled by basic dispel |
| Fear | Forced to move away | Lasts its duration |
| Cyclone | Airborne, no actions | Stun-equivalent, dispelled by strong dispel |

Rules:

- Hard disable cap: 3 hard disables per team in any 10 s window. A fourth is shortened to 0.5 s.
- Purge: basic dispel removes most buffs and root. Strong dispel removes polymorph, silence and cyclone.
- Spell immunity blocks magical damage and disables, not pure damage or HP removal.

### Repost chain (Brainrot original)

A hard disable or ultimate that lands on an enemy starts a repost chain.

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Trigger | Hard disable or ultimate lands on an enemy |
| Radius | 600 |
| Stack effect | +8% attack speed or spell amp per stack |
| Spread | Any ally who damages the target passes a stack to allies within 600 of them |
| Max stacks | 5 |
| Decay | 4 s |

Stacks show as dotted arcs between heroes. Repost arcs are capped at five on screen.

## 9. Launch hero kits
Twenty-four launch heroes, two per archetype. Each has four abilities: three basic and one ultimate. Ultimates unlock at 6, 11 and 16.

### Ability value tiers

Every ability uses one of these tiers. Each hero's abilities are sized to them, with the archetype modifiers in section 21 added on top.

| Ability type | Level 1 | Level 2 | Level 3 | Level 4 | Cooldown (L1 to L4) | Mana (L1 to L4) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Ability 1, damage | 80 | 160 | 240 | 320 | 10, 9, 8, 7 s | 60, 70, 80, 90 |
| Ability 2, control or utility | 2.0 s | 2.5 s | 3.0 s | 3.5 s | 12, 11, 10, 9 s | 70, 80, 90, 100 |
| Ability 3, aura or passive | 300 radius | 350 radius | 400 radius | 450 radius | 14, 12, 10, 8 s | 0 (passive) or 50 |
| Ultimate (unlocks at 6, 11, 16) | 250 damage | 400 damage | 550 damage | n/a (max 3) | 100, 85, 70 s | 150, 200, 250 |

Notes:

- Ultimates have three levels. Each level unlocks at 6, 11 and 16.
- Stun and root durations scale with the ability 2 table. Status resistance (section 21) reduces them.
- Damage numbers are base values. Attribute scaling and item bonuses are added on top.

| Hero | Archetype | Ability 1 | Ability 2 | Ability 3 | Ultimate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Based Fiend | Influencer | Quote Post: three-hit burst, damage scales with Clout | Follower Count: stacks when a nearby enemy dies | Vibes Aura: reduces nearby enemy armor | Viral Thread: lines of damage that feed Go Viral |
| Long-Form Creator | Influencer | Thread: area that damages and slows | Pinned Reply: next attack deals bonus damage | Attention Span: extra attack range | Breaking News: long-range strike |
| Lurk Mode | Lurker | Unseen Mention: strikes from behind while unseen | Dark Mode: cloud that blinds enemies | Cold Open: blinks to a target and attacks | Ghost Post: invisible strike sequence |
| Retargeting | Lurker | Lead Magnet: ranged toss with slow | Cold Outreach: next attack deals bonus damage | Stealth Mode: brief invisibility while moving | Tracked Post: reveals an enemy, gold on hit |
| Who Asked | Reply Guy | Cold Read: freezes the target | Off the Record: fades, briefly invulnerable | Wall of Text: blocks a path | Hot Take Drop: delayed global damage |
| Well Actually | Reply Guy | Citation Needed: slows and damages | Hard Correction: turns the target into a sheep | Drain Thread: drains mana while channeling | Source?: must cite a source to cast |
| Debate Bro | Algorithm-Pilled Carry | Rebuttal: damage per attack and mana drain | Quick Reply: short teleport | Block Button: blocks spell damage | Void Post: damage scales with missing mana |
| Solo Wolf Poster | Algorithm-Pilled Carry | Keyboard Smash: spins and damages nearby enemies | Get Well Soon: heals allies in radius | Crit Happens: chance to critically strike | Doomscroll: rapid strikes that jump between enemies |
| Frost Feed | Doomscroller | Frost Feed: area damage and slow | Hold Still: roots and damages over time | Dark Mode Aura: mana regen for allies | Load More: area nuke around the hero |
| Dragon Scroll | Doomscroller | Dragon Scroll: line of damage | Flash Feed: delayed stun in an area | Hype Meter: attack speed and movement stacks | Viral Clip: single-target burst |
| Read Receipt | Notification Support | Seen Receipt: damage over time | Close Friends Only: protects an ally from death briefly | Push Notification: bounces to nearby units | Bad Vibes: reduces enemy armor |
