## 12. Neutrals, boosts, The Trend and Screenshot
### Jungle camps

Camp types: small, medium, hard and elder. Elders are magic-resistant (not spell-immune).

| Creature | Camp type | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| NPCs | Small | Repeat one voice line. Mirrors the Morning Feed palette |
| Spam | Small | Fast, low HP |
| Shill | Medium | Casts a slowing aura |
| Troll-Bridge | Hard | Blocks a bridge crossing until killed |
| Old Forum Thread | Elder | Long-lived creature, magic-resistant |
| Hot Mic, Echo Chamber, Thread Sprite, Bio Bot, Viral Golem, Cancel Mob, Ratio Hound | Mixed | Stats by camp type, below |

Stacking:

- A camp respawns on the minute if its spawn box is empty.
- Pulling a camp out at about :53 to :55 stacks an extra camp for the next minute.
- Pulling a camp into the lane resets the lane's creep equilibrium.
- Camp stat budgets: Small 300 HP, Medium 550, Hard 950, Elder 1,600, with damage rising one step per tier (UNVERIFIED; section 19 budgets cover heroes, not neutrals).
- Stage camps: the camps beside the river's shallow crossings. A pull made while an enemy hero can see the camp gives +1 Clout per creature killed. Unwatched pulls give normal gold only.

### Boosts

Six listed boosts plus the Algorithm Boost (section 21): seven in total. Two spawn spots on the river; they respawn every 2 min.

| Boost | Effect | Duration |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Sweat Mode | Double damage | 40 s |
| Dank Memes (Haste) | Movement speed boost | 25 s |
| Dank Memes (Illusion) | Spawns an illusion of self | 40 s |
| Dank Memes (Invisibility) | Invisibility until it attacks or casts | 30 s |
| Dank Memes (Regeneration) | Heal over time | 20 s |
| Bounty | Gold and XP on pickup | One-time |

Bounty boosts spawn at the river at game start. Four in total. They give gold and XP, and the initial bounty gives no XP.

### The Trend

A faceless boss built from stacked trending banners.

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| HP | 8,000, plus 175 per minute |
| Magic resistance | 55% |
| Respawn | 8 to 11 min, random |
| Reward | Gold and XP. The killing team picks one of two rotating modifiers for 4 min. The killer takes the Screenshot. |
| Screenshot | One revive at the Spawn Lounge after a 3 s rewind clip. Expires 5 min after pickup. |

### Trend modifiers

Eight modifiers rotate each patch. Two are offered per kill:

| Modifier | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Challenge | +10% move speed for 3 s after each cast |
| Unboxing | −15% item cooldowns |
| Learn to Code | +10% XP from all sources, abilities cost 5% more mana |
| Speedrun | +15% move speed, towers deal +10% damage to you, and your team earns 10% less tower gold |
| Storytime | Channeled abilities finish 25% faster and cost 15% more mana |
| Get Ready With Me | Items bought at the Spawn Lounge cost 10% less. Respawn takes 2 s longer. |
| Algorithm Surge | Clout gain +20%, Clout decay +50% |
| Doomscroll | +8% ability damage while no ally is within 600, -10% move speed |

The modifier shows on the minimap timer and as a team-colored HUD filter for its duration.

### Trend modifier check

Written before any match exists. Each row names who a modifier favors, where it is most likely to dominate, and the cheapest answer. Every row is UNVERIFIED until the checks in section 26 run.

| Modifier | Likely favors | Dominance risk | Answer |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Challenge | Mobile heroes and ganks | High: chase lineups take it every game | Roots, Polymorph and Rescheduled's displace |
| Unboxing | Heroes with short cooldown kits | Low: a flat cooldown cut is easy to plan around | Nothing needed; watch its pick rate |
| Learn to Code | Low-mana heroes who cast rarely | Medium: the mana cost is small for them | Speedrun |
| Speedrun | Aggressive early teams | High: tower damage and speed reward an early rush | Slow the rush; the rusher pays the tower tax |
| Storytime | Channel-heavy heroes (Drain Thread, Mindful Break) | Medium | Channel-free kits |
| Get Ready With Me | Teams that base often | Medium: cheaper items at the Spawn Lounge reward base time | The respawn penalty |
| Algorithm Surge | Clout-scaling heroes | Medium: rewards safe Clout farming | Force fights; decay eats the lead |
| Doomscroll | Assassins and solo laners | High: isolated picks get both bonuses | Group up; the damage bonus turns off |

### Breaking News (event)

Two events per match, at 18:00 and 30:00 (UNVERIFIED). A banner slides in using the Trend banner effect, and a 60 s capture zone opens at the river center.

- **Capture:** a team with heroes inside and no enemy hero inside holds the zone. After 20 s held, its heroes get Front Page for 40 s: Reach +100.
- **Contest:** if both teams have heroes inside, no progress is made.
- **Underdog:** a team in the Underdog mood (section 6) captures at double speed.

Front Page changes Reach only. It does not reveal anyone.

### Screenshot

The Screenshot is held by one hero. The Screenshot expires 5 min after pickup. A hero holding it at the Spawn Lounge can revive once. The revive replays the death as a rewound clip. The Screenshot is the revive reward (Participation Trophy, section 11).

## 13. Vision and fog
Vision decides what the enemy can see, and therefore what they can take. Under Brainrot, enemy vision is also the source of your Clout. Vision is the most-used system in the game.

### Wards

| Ward | Brainrot name | Cost | Duration | Stock | Function |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Vision ward | Lurker Cam | 65 gold | 6 min | Start 2, max 4, restock 150 s | Vision. Enemies see the reveal and earn no Clout. |
| True sight ward | Spoiler Tag | 75 gold | 6 min | Shares a slot with Lurker Cam | True sight. Reveals invisible units and wards. |

- Killing an enemy ward gives 100 gold and 25 XP.
- Enemy wards reveal the area but earn their owner no Clout.
- Towers give true sight at 700 range.

### Reveal tools

| Tool | Brainrot name | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Gem | Gem of Subtext | True sight carried by one hero. Drops on death. |
| Dust | Dust of Receipts | Reveals invisible units in a radius |
| Smoke | Smoke of Deniability | Group invisibility, hidden on the minimap until near an enemy hero or tower. Restock 11 min. |

### Vision states

- **LIVE:** an enemy hero sees you. Clout is earned. The LIVE dot shows on your portrait.
- **Hidden:** no enemy hero sees you. No Clout is earned.
- **Revealed:** an enemy ward or reveal tool shows your position. No Clout is earned.

The LIVE dot is violet with a white ring. It is never red (red means damage).

### Day and night

- The day and night cycle runs 4 min day, 4 min night.
- At night, vision radius drops for every hero. Some heroes have night abilities (Night Shift, Lurk Mode).
- The clock is shown on the minimap as a sun or moon.

### Fog rules

- Clout uses enemy hero vision only. Enemy creeps, towers and wards do not count.
- A stealthed hero is revealed by true sight, reveal tools and any enemy hero within 300 range.
- Invisibility from items and abilities is broken when the hero attacks, casts or takes damage (per item).

## 14. Draft and modes
The draft is the first decision of the match. It sets the hero pool, the lane plan and the item plan.

### Game modes

| Mode | Use | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Showrunner Draft | Ranked and main | Two captains ban and pick in turn. 30 s per pick, 130 s bonus time per team. |
| Open Feed | Casual | Each player picks freely. No bans. |
| Algorithm Draft | Casual | Heroes drawn from a 50-hero pool. |
| Shuffle Draft | Casual | Each player picks from a random 10-hero set. |
| Ranked Open Feed | Ranked | Each player nominates a hero, then half the nominated heroes are banned at random. |
| Short Form | Casual or ranked, 25 minute target | Two lanes per side, mid removed. Trend opens at 5:00. Original Post falls once both T2s on a lane are down. Surrender vote at 15 min. Details in the Short Form section below. UNVERIFIED |

### Showrunner Draft order

Ten bans and ten picks, alternating by team. The order (final order):

1. Ban: 1st, 2nd, 1st, 2nd
2. Pick: 1st, 2nd, 2nd, 1st
3. Ban: 2nd, 1st, 2nd, 1st
4. Pick: 2nd, 1st, 2nd, 1st
5. Ban: 2nd, 1st
6. Pick: 1st, 2nd

### Short Form

Short Form is the same game on a smaller map. All numbers are UNVERIFIED.

- Two lanes per side (top and bottom). Mid lane and its tower and Content Mill rows are removed.
- The Trend opens at 5:00 and respawns in 4 to 6 min.
- Original Post is invulnerable until both T2s on a lane fall, not both T4s.
- XP per level is multiplied by 1.5 for the same level thresholds.
- Clout gain, Reach, Stan and the Repost chain work as in the full game.

### Roles

| Position | Role | Lane | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Carry | Safe lane | Clout carry or late-game damage |
| 2 | Mid | Mid | Highest-impact solo lane |
| 3 | Offlane | Off lane | Initiator, tank or disruptor |
| 4 | Roamer | Safe lane, with carry | Soft support, gank pressure |
| 5 | Hard support | Safe lane, with carry | Vision, protection, Stan support |

Jungler is a viable role for heroes with camp-clearing kits (Comment Leech, Touch-Grass Hermit, Lurker archetype). A jungler is a position choice, not a sixth slot.

### Archetype lanes

Lane preference by archetype. This is guidance for the draft UI, not a restriction.

- Carry: Algorithm-Pilled Carry, Influencer, Doomscroller
- Mid: Doomscroller, Ghost Account, Hot Take
- Offlane: Moderator, Hot Take
- Roamer: Lurker, Reply Guy, Parasocial
- Hard support: Notification Support, Archivist

### Ban phase

- Bans are hidden until the phase ends, then revealed together.
- A banned hero cannot be picked by either team for the match.
- Pick and ban rates are tracked for balance (section 19).

### Pick screen

The pick screen is titled "Draft your content plan." It shows the archetype role icon on every hero, and the Trend modifier for the match once it is known.

