## 16. Humor and tone
The register is maximalist, meme-forward and then some. Two images carry two readings. The second reading is the punchline.

### Rules

1. Jokes target observed behavior: posting, reposting, ratios, moderation.
2. Jokes never sit on the gameplay read path. A signal (LIVE, Stan, Go Viral, Ratio) is always readable without its joke.
3. Voice is calm and under-acted. Nothing shouts except the Hot Take archetype, and that is also a joke.
4. Gags are always on. They never sit on the read path, so nothing needs a switch.
5. Meme vocabulary is generic internet usage only (cope, ratio, based, touch grass, NPC). No brand names, named creators, franchise characters or owned catchphrases. Any phrase can rotate out per patch.
6. Loaded phrases (cope, seethe, mald, skill issue, cry about it, L + ratio, ok boomer, learn to code) are allowed in the Loaded tier. They aim at in-game play, never at a person's identity: no slurs, no group-targeting slogans, no real people or events. There is no switch: the game is loaded on purpose.

### Gags

| # | Gag | System | Trigger | Fade or opt-out |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 01 | Loading fold-in: two outer panels slide together, revealing the first Trend modifier. Caption: What is everyone talking about this match? | The Trend | Every load | Skippable. Static in Reduced Motion. |
| 02 | Stan signs: hand-lettered signs held by buffed creeps, naming the buffing hero with a misspelling that rotates each match | Stan and Reach | Zoom or spectator camera | Signs stay. Misspelling rotates. |
| 03 | Via shrinkage: each Repost link adds a small via tag. By the fifth link the original is too small to read. | Repost | Chain of 3 or more | Spectator and hover only |
| 04 | Death recap as analytics: header Your post was ratioed. Killers listed as Top replies. Line: Engagement redistributed: 50%. | Ratio | Death | Standard damage table first. |
| 05 | Rebrand record: hero name followed by a small grey formerly tag | Rebrand | Rebrand | Death recap or victory screen, at most once per match |
| 06 | Go Private blinds: windows show the padlock and the blinds drop. One slat stays bent open. | Go Private | Activation | Cosmetic. The padlock is the read. |
| 07 | Stale Trend husk: the expired modifier's costume lies in the pit until the Trend respawns | The Trend | Kill | Fades on respawn |
| 08 | Out-of-bounds margins: a creep sits on grass with eyes closed. A lone tree carries a no signal glyph. | Map edge | Camera at edge | Static and silent |
| 09 | Item flavor lines in deadpan (section 11) | Items | Tooltip hover | Hidden in compact tooltips |
| 10 | Recommended banner: appears on a lane the algorithm favors, reading Recommended for you, with Based on your activity in small print | Lane notice | Lane selection | Small print |
| 11 | Victory and defeat fold: click and hold reveals the losing Original Post as \[deleted\] | Original Post | End screen | Requires a click. Clean stats view is the default. |
| 12 | Go Viral shadow counter: the hero's own shadow shows a ticking follower count | Go Viral | Activation | Self and allies only. Reduced opacity. |
| 13 | Chat, is this real?: a kill taken at under 10% HP flashes that caption over the killer's portrait | Kills | Kill at under 10% HP | 1.5 s, portrait only, once per 2 min. |
| 14 | NPC loop: NPC camp creatures repeat one grey speech bubble when pulled: Nice weather today. | Jungle camps | Pull | Fades in 2 s. |
| 15 | Copium wears off: when Bottle of Copium ends, the portrait takes a 0.5 s grey flash captioned Reality. | Bottle of Copium | Item ends | Portrait only. |
| 16 | Learn to code: a hero who dies to their own ability, item or tower-aggro mistake gets a grey death-recap footnote reading Have you tried learning to code? | Death recap | Self-inflicted death | Footnote only. |
| 17 | Lives rent free: the hero who killed you gets a tiny house icon next to their scoreboard name for 2 min, and a dotted line to your portrait | Scoreboard | Death | Self only. Cosmetic. Never hides a stat. |
| 18 | Nobody: / Me: loading tip format. Tips alternate between plain and two-line Nobody: / Me: jokes about the match's Trend modifier | Loading screen | Every load | Skippable. |
| 19 | Mald meter: a hero who dies three times in a row gets a small steam puff over the portrait | Deaths | Third death in a row | Portrait only. |
| 20 | Cancelled stamp: a hero who dies while Viral gets a red-free grey CANCELLED stamp on the scoreboard row for 5 s. Rebrand swaps it for Rebranded. | Go Viral, Rebrand | Death while Viral | Scoreboard only. |
| 21 | Touch grass: a hero standing at the Spawn Lounge for 60 s sprouts a patch of grass at their feet and a tiny sun | Spawn Lounge idle | 60 s at Spawn Lounge | Cosmetic. Never in a fight. |

### Running bit

The formerly tag (gag 05) is the running joke. Its rules and sample lines are in plan/23-voice-and-banter.md.

