| Doomscroller | Slow +10% / Root +1 s | Mana regen +1 / Cooldown −15 s | Puddle on ground / Damage +50% | Every second cast / +10% vs Clout heroes |
| Notification Support | Damage over time +2 / Shield +1 s | Bounce +1 / Armor −2 | Spreads on death / Heal 20% | Worse effect / Reveal 3 s |
| Moderator | Slow +1 s / Shield +50 | Radius +50 / Stun +0.5 s | Reflect 10% / Mark for allies | Stun on death / 1 Clout per 200 damage absorbed |
| Ghost Account | Slow +10% / Cooldown −2 s | Stealth +1 s / Crit +50% | Leaves a decoy / Not revealed | Double Clout / Name hidden on death |
| Hot Take | Length +100 / Attack speed +10% | Stun +0.3 s / Extra target | Stun 0.5 s / Heal allies | Global / Reveal 2 s |
| Archivist | Radius +30 / Duration +0.5 s | Range +100 / Duration +1 s | Two charges / Reveals a Clout pulse | Detonates on death / LIVE for 2 s |
| Parasocial | Speed +10% / Duration +1 s | Damage +50 / Stun +0.5 s | Orb returns / Leaves a copy | Repeats on death / Extends for allied Clout |
| Touch-Grass Hermit | Radius +50 / Cooldown −5 s | Treant +1 / Range +200 | Root +0.5 s / Treants heal | Clout from Go Outside / Regen +2% unseen |

### Backpack

Three backpack slots, indexed 7 to 9. Backpack items give their passive stats. Active items do not work from the backpack. Sell-back rules match the inventory.

### Neutral items

- One neutral item slot per hero. It sits outside the six inventory slots and the backpack.
- Neutral items drop from jungle camps. A hero gets one choice of three. A new neutral replaces the old one.
- Tier timings: tier 1 from 7:00, tier 2 from 17:00, tier 3 from 27:00, tier 4 from 37:00.

| Tier | Source | Items (choose one of three) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Small camps | Thread Pin: +10 damage. Crumb Pouch: +1.5 HP regen. NPC Badge: +8% spell amplification. |
| 2 | Medium camps | Echo Ring: 8% attack lifesteal. Stan Sign: allied creeps in Reach gain +5% damage. Hot Mic: 15% chance on attack to silence for 0.6 s. |
| 3 | Hard camps | Viral Bell: 10% chance on attack to heal 60 HP. Ratio Cloak: 8% damage reduction above 50 Clout. Cancel Mask: +6% magic resistance, +50 max mana. |
| 4 | Old Forum Thread | Eternal Thread: +150 HP, +20 damage, 10% faster cooldowns. Vintage Post: active, 2 s reveal and 1.5 s stun in 400 radius, 60 s cooldown. Long Tail: +25% Clout gain. |

### Safe Spots

- Two Safe Spots per team, one at each river crossing next to the team's safe lane. Available from 0:00.
- Active: heals all allies within 500 radius for 14% of max HP per second, for 5 s.
- Cooldown 45 s, shared per Safe Spot.

### Lite Plan

- Cost 1,400 gold. A standalone item, not built from Pro Plan.
- Adds one second effect to a basic ability on the holder. The effect is set per hero in section 9.
- Stacks with Pro Plan.

### Decoy Posts

- Fifteen Decoy Post buildings per base. Each has 500 HP, no armor and a 5 gold bounty.
- Decoy Posts do not count toward tiers or the win condition. Creeps do not target them.

### Stat Boost

- A fifth skill. It takes unspent ability points, after the three basic skills and the ultimate are maxed.
- Each point gives +2 to all three attributes. Maximum 10 points.

### Chat Check

- Reveals enemy heroes within 900 radius for 8 s.
- Shared team cooldown of 270 s. Any hero on the team can cast it.

### Status resistance

- Base 0%. Items and talents add it.
- Reduces the duration of stuns, silences, roots, polymorphs, fear and taunts. Cap 50%.

### Algorithm Boost

- Spawns with the other boosts on the river. Lasts 50 s.
- While held: Reach +100 and a violet pip on the minimap. No cooldown or mana change.

### Gamer Fuel

- The Trend drops Gamer Fuel on its second kill and every kill after.
- Gamer Fuel cannot be sold. Chug it to restore 2,500 HP and 1,000 mana over 4 s. One can per drop.

### Pit Boss (roster entry 112)

- **Name:** Pit Boss. Archetype: Moderator. Attribute: Strength. Range: Melee.
- **Gag:** Runs the pit. Has never been to it.
- **Ability 1, Pit Post:** area trap in 400 radius that roots and damages.
- **Ability 2, Atrophy Feed:** aura that damages nearby enemies, growing by 10% per second in combat.
- **Ability 3, Gate Crash:** places a gate at a point. Allies who step through teleport to the other gate.
- **Ultimate, Hard Fork:** teleports an ally to a point, then damages enemies around the arrival.

### Signature mechanics

Each of these heroes has one rule that makes its kit read differently on the map. Each rule uses only Reach, reveal, Stan, Repost, Clout, the scoreboard or vision, never a stat. Numbers are UNVERIFIED.

| Hero | Signature mechanic | Clout tie |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lurk Mode | Lurk Meter: 8 s unseen charges one free Unseen Mention. | Unseen play |
| Retargeting | Tracked Post marks a target; its LIVE state shows to the whole team as a counter. | Vision |
| Who Asked | Cold Read freezes targets with more Clout than Who Asked; others are only slowed. | Clout |
| Well Actually | Source? casts only while one ally on its team is LIVE. | Vision |
| Debate Bro | Rebuttal cuts the target's Reach by 100 for 6 s. | Reach |
| Solo Wolf Poster | Reach +50 every 10 s with no ally within 600, up to +150. | Reach |
| Frost Feed | When a rooted target dies, the root jumps to the nearest Clout hero within 300. | Clout |
| Dragon Scroll | Each Hype Meter stack adds Reach +20. | Reach |
| Read Receipt | Seen Receipt shows its team each enemy's last seen position for 10 s. | Vision |
| Mentions | Public Apology gives a pinged ally Stan radius +100 for 5 s. | Stan |
| Moderator | A Warning-marked target loses half its Reach. | Reach |
| Ban Hammer | Gavel Slam reveals its target to the whole team for 2 s. | Reveal |
| Anonymous Poster | Anon Mode hides its Clout on the scoreboard. | Scoreboard |
| Ban Evader | Clones inherit Reach but not Clout. | Clout |
| Hot Take | Each hard disable it lands gives its team Reach +50 for 10 s. | Reach |
| Yell at Clouds | Yell sets the taunted enemy's Reach to 0 while taunted. | Reach |
| Mods | A hero standing in a Final Warning trap is revealed to its team. | Reveal |
| Hook Guy | A hooked hero loses Reach while hooked. | Reach |
| Looping Clip | Its stun repeats each time the target goes LIVE again. | Vision |
| Comeback Tour | On revive, Reach +200 for 10 s. | Reach |

### Seasons

A season is one patch. Each season rotates three things and changes no numbers:

- The Trend modifier pool (section 12).
- The phrase pool for the announcer and chat wheel (sections 16 and 18).
- The cosmetic skin theme: costumes, plinths and the Trend banner.

Numbers change only in the balance pass.

### Spectator reactions

- Spectators send reactions from the chat wheel (section 18). Each viewer has a 10 s cooldown per reaction.
- Reactions show to spectators only. They have no effect on play.
- Ranked matches show no spectator reactions on the player screen.

## 22. Art direction

Visual direction for the 112 heroes (roster 001 to 111 plus Pit Boss 112), the 96 launch abilities (24 heroes), the 50 item rows in section 11, and the eight Trend modifiers in section 12. Shape, value and color rules come from section 17. Archetypes come from section 15.

## Rules used in every table

- **Body codes.** P1 taller (+10% height). P2 broader (+15% width). P3 compact (-10% height). P4 longer (+15% length). P5 short legs (-20% leg length). P6 big head (+20% head size). All percentages are design targets, UNVERIFIED.
- **Value groups.** Written as body / head / prop, using L (light), M (mid) and D (dark). Head and prop each differ from body by the 30% luminance delta in section 17. Mapping: L about 85%, M about 55%, D about 25% luminance, all UNVERIFIED.
- **Primary value group** is the body value.
- **Sibling rule.** Within an archetype, take the hero's 0-based index k in roster order. Body code is P(k mod 6 + 1). Body value is L, M, D for floor(k/6) = 0, 1, 2. Every prop in an archetype is unique. Any two siblings therefore differ in prop silhouette and in at least one of body code or body value, which meets the two-of-three rule in section 15.
- **Accent shifts** are named steps from the archetype accent. No hex is set here.
- **Color guards.** Keep off #A35CFF (Clout only), red (damage only), #2E8BFF and #FF8A1F (team colors), and #3DDC97 (heal). Hot Take ember and Parasocial rose shift off red. Notification green-cyan shifts off heal green. Ghost lavender stays low in saturation so it does not read as Clout. Influencer violet trim uses the LIVE violet, not the Clout hex.

