## 2. Single source of truth and generation direction

**Canonical data.** One TSV per table, UTF-8, LF, header row, stable id column. The canonical files are `scenarios/brainrot/data/*.tsv`, which the pack ships, so they hold Brainrot names only. Headers, as an illustration:

```
heroes.tsv     hero_id slug name archetype_id attr range launch status
abilities.tsv  hero_id slot slug name kind tier dmg_r1 dmg_r2 dmg_r3 dmg_r4 cd_r1 cd_r2 cd_r3 cd_r4 mana_r1 mana_r2 mana_r3 mana_r4 ult_gate_1 ult_gate_2 ult_gate_3 status
items.tsv      item_id slug name kind tier cost components stats active stock restock_s drop_on_death flavor status
```

**Generated outputs, one direction only.**

1. `scenarios/brainrot/*.osd` and a key=value rules file, written by `scenarios/brainrot/tools/gen.mjs`. The `tools/` folder is excluded from Pages by `layout-site.sh` line 26.
2. The markdown tables in `247420/plan/NN-*.md`, written by the same tool. It finds each table by its heading text. It does not use HTML comment markers, because the comment rule in the global instructions (INVARIANT 3) applies to comments in files.
3. A drift check: the tool regenerates everything and fails if the tree differs. This copies the determinism check already in `tests.yml`.

Direction: TSV to `.osd`, TSV to the rules file, TSV to plan markdown. Nothing flows back. Before the first generation the plan markdown is the source, so the first TSV is produced once from it and reviewed. After that cutover, a number is typed only in the TSV.

**Rules for ids and names.**

- `hero_id`, `item_id`, `archetype_id` and `modifier_id` are append-only numbers. They are never reused. The generator sorts by these ids, never by plan order.
- Engine name = `slug`, which must match `[a-z][a-z0-9_]*`, be at most 32 bytes for hero slugs (the wire's pick-name limit), and be unique within each name list.
- A rename changes the `name` column only. Changing a `slug` is an engine rename, done once, in the generator.
- The `status` column is `UNVERIFIED` (default), `checked:<repo path>` (only when a 6.88g value matched locally), or `design` (set by the balance pass). The generator prints it next to every number, which is the AGENTS.md rule that unknowns stay marked in the file that holds the value.

**Units.** Numbers are typed in plan units: seconds, percent, gold and game units. The generator converts. Seconds become ticks at 16 per second, rounded (3.8 s is 60.8 ticks, so 61). Percentages become Q16 (65536 equals 1.0). Distance is in game units, the engine whole-unit scale: 1 game unit is 125/8 milli-units (section 20, decision 24).

**Pack location.** Option A is `scenarios/brainrot/`. It ships automatically through `cp -r scenarios`, but it needs `mapexport` lines added to `stage.sh`, `pages.yml` and `ci.yml`. Option B is `247420/pack/`, which needs a copy line in `layout-site.sh`. Use B for the first slice; move to A when the pack wiring lines land.

## 3. Smallest first-playable slice: data files

The slice is file 26: six heroes, two modifiers, a fixed draft order, one stage camp per side, Clout, mood, Breaking News and the Short Form map. Row counts are what the slice needs.

| File | Rows | Compiles to | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `manifest.json` | 1 | pack root | modules, image name, tables, rules file |
| `heroes.tsv` | 6 | unit rows | Based Fiend, Lurk Mode, Moderator, Hot Take, Mentions, Mods |
| `abilities.tsv` | 24 | ability, SKIL and AXTN rows | four slots each |
| `items.tsv` | 6 | item rows | Lurker Cam, Spoiler Tag, Anon Mask, Confident Answer, Sticky Note and Ring Light (components of Lurker Cam). Rebrand is an action, not an item (section 5). |
| `modifiers.tsv` | 2 | Lua rule | Challenge and Learn to Code |
| `rules.tsv` | about 30 | rules file | Clout: Viral at 100, 20 s, 25 after, cap 200, decay. Reach: 300 base, plus 3 per Clout, cap 600. Stan: +20% damage, +2 armor. Repost: cap 5, +8%, radius 600, 4 s decay. Ratio: 50%. |
| `moods.tsv` | 3 | Lua | Front Runner, Underdog and Even (file 06) |
| `events.tsv` | 1 | Lua | Breaking News zone rules (file 12) |
| `camps.tsv` | 2 | `spawn(...)` | one stage camp per side (file 26) |
| `draft_order.tsv` | 1 mode | lobby | fixed pick order for the slice |
| `lines.tsv` | about 12 | UI JSON and Lua | kill, Ratio, Clout 100 and Rebrand lines (file 16) |
| map | 1 | `map.osd` and `routes.osd` | Short Form (file 14): two lanes per side, river, both bases |

Code the slice also needs, which is not data: the Clout state machine, Reach, Ratio on death with the 200 cap, Repost, Stan, the mood check, the Breaking News capture rule, and Rebrand. All of it is Lua hooks under the 2,500-step budget per call (docs/MODDING.md).

## 4. Which plan numbers can be checked against 6.88g today

**Short answer: none can be confirmed today.** The archive is not on this machine (A3). The pairing between plan names and 6.88g rows lives in `247420/internal/parity-map.md`. For this note only its counts were read, and no name from it was copied: about 110 hero rows against 112 roster entries, 94 launch-ability rows against 96 slots, and 31 item rows. That file is tracked in git but never copied into the pack or Pages, so CI can read it and the build cannot ship it.

| Plan number | Section | Repo value and where it sits | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Starting gold 600 | 5, 20 (Q2) | `scenarios/moba/economy.osd`: `opening_resource_a=625`, commented as recalled, not read from a dump | UNVERIFIED. Plan and repo disagree (600 against 625). Neither is from 6.88g in the repo. |
| Passive income 1 gold per second | 5, 20 (Q3) | No matching field in `economy.osd` | UNVERIFIED |
| XP totals at levels 2, 5, 10, 15, 20, 25: 200, 1400, 5400, 11900, 20900, 32400 | 5 | `scenarios/moba/tuning.osd` `xp_curve` has the same six values at the same levels. The file says the 6.88g data holds no experience table and the values were recalled. | UNVERIFIED. Agreement with an unverified value is not evidence. |
| Base HP 200, mana 50, speed 300 and 522, ranges 150 and 500, attack times 1.7 and 1.5, turn 0.6, magic resistance 25% | 7 | The repo has per-hero rows (`heroes_688g.tsv`, `units_heroes.osd`), and `docs/REFERENCE.md` marks the rows it shows as UNVERIFIED. The plan block is a rule, not a row, so there is no row to compare it with. | UNVERIFIED. Needs pairing. |
| Tower HP 1300, 1600, 1600, 2200; tower gold 160 to 280 | 3, 5 | Tower rows are keyed by role in `units.osd`. The convergence report says role keys do not pair by name. | UNVERIFIED |
| Item costs (Lurker Cam 65 up to Rapier 6000) | 11 | Item costs in `items.osd` come from the third-party dump, not 6.88g (docs/CONVERGENCE_688G.md, intro) | UNVERIFIED |
| Trend HP 8000, plus 175 per minute; magic resistance 55% | 12 | The repo has a boss row from 6.88g (section 8 of the convergence report). Pairing needs the map. | UNVERIFIED |
| Clout, Ratio, Repost, Go Viral, Stan values | 6, 8 | Brainrot originals. A classic archive cannot contain them. | UNVERIFIED by construction |
| Ability value tiers (damage 80 to 320, cooldowns, mana) | 9 | Repo ability rows are original-game values, all UNVERIFIED in REFERENCE.md | UNVERIFIED |
| Ultimate unlocks at 6, 11, 16 | 7, 9 | FORMAT.md fixes ultimate gates at 6, 12, 18 (SKIL) | Conflict between plan and format, not a 6.88g question. See R4. |

To make a check possible: (1) have the owner supply the archive, (2) run `convert-688g-map.mjs` with the archive path as an argument, not a machine path, (3) pair locally against the map, (4) write `checked:<path>` into the matching `status` cells. Step 3 cannot run in CI until the map is tracked.

## 5. Risks and open questions

### Risks

- **R1. The parity map stays out of packs and Pages.** `layout-site.sh` copies `scenarios/`, `mods/` and `js/client/`, not `247420/`, so the map does not ship today.
- **R2. The plan is tracked but outside the build.** `plan/` and `internal/` are tracked in git; `layout-site.sh` does not copy them. Drift checks can read them in CI, but generated plan tables are never shipped.
- **R3. Pack wiring is hard-coded.** `stage.sh` line 16, `pages.yml` lines 91 to 92 and `ci.yml` lines 89 to 90 list the packs by name. A new pack without these edits gets no `.osdt`, and `layout-site.sh` still succeeds because it checks only moba (A2).
- **R4. Ultimate gates differ.** FORMAT.md line 307 fixes ultimate gates at 6, 12 and 18. Plan sections 7 and 9 say 6, 11 and 16. This needs a format decision (which bumps the version) or a plan change.
- **R5. Time units do not divide evenly.** Ticks run at 16 per second (REFERENCE.md line 5), and FORMAT.md requires durations as integer ticks. The plan's 3.8 s per level gives 60.8 ticks. The generator needs a written rounding rule.
- **R6. Clout, Reach, Stan, Ratio, Repost and global Trend modifiers have no data slot.** ITEM_STATS is fixed at 38 entries (FORMAT.md line 298), and plan decision 9 says Clout is never a stat, so these are Lua hooks. AXTN modifiers (8 per ability, FORMAT.md line 328) cannot express a global modifier. Each hook runs under a 2,500-step budget (docs/MODDING.md line 47), which constrains per-tick Reach recalculation.
- **R7. Filter bits are capped.** FNAM allows at most 15 bits (FORMAT.md line 376). Twelve archetype filters plus role filters can exhaust that. Keep archetype as a data column and use filter bits only for targeting.
- **R8. Ids are positions.** Item ids are record indices, and ability indices follow declaration order (FORMAT.md). Unit `kind` is a `u16` position on the wire. Inserting a row renumbers everything after it, which makes a new image hash and a SWAP at a tick (docs/WIRE.md). Generation must keep ids stable, as section 2 says.
- **R9. Output must be byte-stable.** `tests.yml` compares two `mapexport` runs byte for byte. The generator must sort, use LF, fix float formatting and write no timestamps.
- **R10. FORMAT.md is internally inconsistent.** It says "the reader requires all twenty-eight tags" (line 28), but the header, the table and the rule at line 17 all say 27. Fix the sentence when the file is next edited.
- **R11. Contradictions found on 2026-10-25, resolved on 2026-10-27.**
  - The component 1 band is 50 to 100, the finished Tier 1 band is 65 to 300, and assembly is explicitly discounted (file 11).
  - Spoiler Tag moved to Tier 1 at 75 gold (file 11).
  - Drain Blade, Grindset and Lite Plan gained roster rows; Drain Blade and Lite Plan gained stats rows (file 11).
  - File 12 now names eight Trend modifiers, with check rows for all eight.
  - Files 10 and 15 still use short archetype labels ("Algorithm", "Ghost", "Notification", "Hermit") while files 09, 14 and 19 use the full names. The TSV `alias` column carries both.
  - Rebrand is an action, not an item (file 05); file 26 matches.
  - `00-index.md` lists files 00 to 26 and its links resolve (checked 2026-10-27).
- **R12. The source is moving.** During this session files 06, 11, 12 and 14 changed, and files 22, 23, 24 and 26 were added. Generators must find tables by heading and must reject duplicate or missing headings.
- **R13. The 6.88g archive is absent.** The convert tools cannot run here, so the derived tables cannot be regenerated from the source. The local checkout and origin/main matched on 2026-10-27.
- **R14. Local changes are uncommitted.** `scripts/dev/stage.sh` and several `js/client` files were modified at session start. The `stage.sh` facts in A2 come from the working tree.
- **R15. Measured mismatch in the scenario data.** The convergence report counts 366 differing field comparisons (docs/CONVERGENCE_688G.md section 3). The scenario stats are therefore not 6.88g values even where names pair.

### Open questions

1. **Plan distance unit: resolved 2026-10-27.** Distances are game units; 1 game unit is 125/8 milli-units (section 20, decision 24).
2. **Starting gold: resolved.** 600, per section 20, decision 14; the repo 625 changes to match.
3. **Pack location: resolved.** The slice pack lives at `247420/pack/`; it moves to `scenarios/brainrot/` once the pack wiring lines land (R3).
4. **Power tiers and budgets: resolved.** Power-tier letters are withdrawn (decision 20). Archetype budgets are inputs written by the balance pass.
5. **Rebrand: resolved.** An action (file 05), never an item.
6. **Trend modifiers: resolved.** Eight, with Algorithm Surge and Doomscroll added (file 12).
7. **Missing rows: resolved.** Drain Blade, Grindset and Lite Plan have rows; Spoiler Tag is Tier 1 (file 11).
8. **Name collision: resolved.** Archetypes have no engine name list; the hero slug `moderator` keeps its name.
9. **Who sets `checked`: resolved.** The build owner runs the local pairing and writes `checked:`; no CI job can.
10. **Archive access: open.** The owner supplies `reference map 6.88g.w3x`, which is still absent (A3), so section 4 cannot run.

## Method and limits

- Searches used gm `codesearch` (literal and filename modes), `fs_readdir`, `fs_read` and `exec_js` for counting plan tables. The 2026-10-27 revision ran `git status` and `git rev-list` only; no repo file outside `247420/` was edited.
- Gm search problems encountered are listed in the report to the caller, not here.

## 26. First playable, cut list and checks

The first playable tests what is unique before it tests the classic MOBA basics. Every number here is UNVERIFIED until a build runs the checks below.

## First playable slice

**Goal:** show that Clout, the Algorithm mood and the Trend modifiers make matches different, and that the rest of the game can be built on top.

| Area | In the slice |
| --- | --- |
| Map | Short Form layout (section 14): two lanes per side, the river, both bases, one stage camp per side. |
| Heroes | Six: Based Fiend (Influencer), Lurk Mode (Lurker), Moderator (Moderator), Hot Take (Hot Take), Mentions (Notification Support), Mods (Archivist). One per archetype group. |
| Clout | Earn, decay, Reach, Go Viral, Ratio on death with the 200 cap. |
| Mood | Front Runner, Underdog and Even (section 6). |
| Events | Breaking News, two events per match (section 12); the slice runs the 18:00 one. |
| Modifiers | Two from the pool: Challenge and Learn to Code. |
| Items | Lurker Cam, Spoiler Tag, Anon Mask, Confident Answer. |
| Presentation | LIVE dot, Clout bar, death recap (Ratio), Rebrand record, announcer lines for kills and Ratio. |

**Not in the slice:** Showrunner Draft (draft is a fixed pick order for the slice), the full talent trees, neutral items, Decoy Posts, Safe Spots, Stat Boost, Chat Check, Go Private, Pit Boss, Seasons, spectator reactions, the other 18 heroes.

**Exit criteria:** the runnable checks below pass across at least 200 matches (UNVERIFIED), and the eight playtest scenarios each record a result.

## Cut list

| Item | v1 | Later | Why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Heroes | 6 | 24 launch, then 112 | Test the mechanics before the roster. |
| Boosts | Algorithm Boost, Bounty, Dank Memes (Haste) | Dank Memes (Illusion, Invisibility, Regeneration), Sweat Mode | Fewer boosts make the Clout effects easier to read. |
| Trend modifiers | 2 | 8 | Compare two before adding more. |
| Talents | None | Full sets from section 21 | Power growth comes after the base kits are tested. |
| Neutral items | None | Section 21 | Tested after camps are proven. |
| Decoy Posts, Safe Spots, Stat Boost | None | Section 21 | Not needed to test Clout. |
| Chat Check | None | Section 21 | Vision is covered by wards. |
| Go Private | None | Section 3 | Building defence is tested later. |
| Repost chain | Yes, cap 5 stacks | Full rules | It is a pillar, so it is included at full cap. |
| Gags | Death recap, Rebrand record, announcer | All others | Gags are presentation, not balance. |
| Seasons and spectator reactions | None | Section 21 | Not part of a test. |

## Playtest scenarios

Run each scenario in the build. Record the result, the time taken and any sign that a rule was unreadable.

1. **Clout comeback.** One team gets 300 Clout ahead for 30 s. Does the Front Runner mood show on the minimap, and does the Underdog catch-up feel fair? Pass: the mood flips and flips back with no flicker inside 30 s.
2. **Lurk ambush.** Lurk Mode waits unseen for 8 s, then uses Unseen Mention. Can a player see from the screen alone that it was unseen? Pass: no LIVE dot, and the state reads without text.
3. **Ratio cap.** A hero dies with 200 or more Clout. Pass: no more than 200 Clout moves, and the split goes to the killer and assists.
4. **Trend modifier fight.** Challenge and Learn to Code both on offer. Pass: the result is logged for the modifier check in section 12.
5. **Breaking News contest.** Both teams have heroes in the zone. Pass: no capture progress is made.
6. **Stage camp.** The same pull is made watched and unwatched. Pass: only the watched pull gives Clout.
7. **Rebrand while Viral.** A Viral hero dies. Pass: the CANCELLED stamp shows, and Rebrand swaps it for Rebranded.
8. **Read check.** Grayscale and each colorblind preset show LIVE, Stan, Ratio and Repost. Pass: each signal is readable without its color.

## Runnable checks

Each check has an ID, an input, an output and a threshold. Thresholds come from section 19.

| ID | Check | Input | Output | Pass |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| C1 | Modifier win rate | Matches grouped by picked modifier | Win rate per modifier | 45 to 55% for each |
| C2 | Modifier pick rate | Offers and picks | Share of offers picked | At most 65% |
| C3 | Breaking News contest | Matches with both teams in the zone | Capture progress made | Zero |
| C4 | Mood flicker | Mood flips with timestamps | Flips within 30 s of the last flip | Zero |
| C5 | Ratio cap | Ratio events | Clout moved per death | At most 200 |
| C6 | Disable cap | Hard disables per team | Fourth disable in any 10 s window | Shortened to 0.5 s every time |
| C7 | Snowball | Matches with a 10,000 gold deficit | Comeback rate | At least 10% |
| C8 | Rename regression | Win rate before and after a rename | Difference in points | Within 1 point |
| C9 | Chat mute | Mutes in the first 10 minutes | Share of players | Rotate the phrase pool above 25% |
| C10 | Breaking News capture rate | Captures per event | Capture rate | Track only; no threshold yet |

The Clout-only rule (decision 9 in section 20) is checked by reading the effect text of every Clout effect. It is not a runtime check.

